    "narrative": "For May 20, 2026, the Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (82.34) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98), both of whom capitalize on high-upside matchups against favorable arms. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a strong R/R platoon edge against Tyler Mahle and a high xwOBA, while **Mickey Moniak** is positioned for a massive day at the plate due to the combination of a hitter-friendly venue and the slow delivery of Jack Leiter, which significantly boosts his stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor for our 5x5 Roto standing. **James Wood** also earns a strong start (64.60) by securing the leadoff spot against a lefty; while neutral platoon splits are usually a concern, the Order #1 boost pushes his efficiency well into our \"Strong\" tier.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card was leaving **Cole Young** (42.51) on the bench. While his score is bolstered by favorable park factors and the stolen base potential presented by the opposing pitcher\u2019s delivery, he was ultimately pushed out by the higher-tier upside of **Zach McKinstry** and **Brice Turang**. We are also closely monitoring the lineup pending status for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Dalton Rushing**, whose efficiency scores could swing if they are dropped further down the order. Furthermore, we continue to exercise caution with **Seiya Suzuki** (53.40); despite a decent base, the combination of a tough lefty starter and wind-in conditions at the park makes him a marginal play that we are keeping on the fringe to preserve our game caps.",
